<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean Daelim wins $160 mln India project.</title>
<headline>S.Korean Daelim wins $160 mln India project.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daelim Engineering Co Ltd said on Wednesday it had won a $160 million order to build petrochemical plants in India for India's Haldia Petrochemical Ltd.  </p>
<p>A company statement said the project included a 210,000 tonne-a-year polypropylene plant and a 200,000 tonne-a-year high density polyethylene plant in a petrochemical complex in West Bengal, India.</p>
<p>The project, which was awarded on a turnkey basis, is scheduled to be completed in May 1999.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
